cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use nook, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "nook: an agent-first, read-only Airbnb search + availability CLI"
abstract: >-
  nook is a read-only, JSON-first command-line tool for searching public, logged-out Airbnb
  listings and dumping a forward per-day availability calendar, engineered to be driven by LLM
  agents: stable versioned output schema, machine-readable self-description, semantic exit codes,
  token-bounded output, prompt-injection fencing of untrusted text, and a persistent, cross-process
  politeness throttle with a circuit breaker. Booking is deliberately out of scope.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wolfe
    given-names: Ryan
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/rnwolfe/nook"
url: "https://github.com/rnwolfe/nook"
keywords:
  - airbnb
  - cli
  - agent
  - llm
  - availability
  - search
  - travel
